                                "example_id": "3bc17058-675f-44c6-b26d-62e3e807bba0",
                                "sense_id": "758cb6c9-cffe-3f71-aa40-eec3794b5795",
                                "text": "Ever, as on they bore, more loud / And louder rung the pibroch proud."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5535b079-8417-4265-abed-658a30efdeed",
                                "sense_id": "758cb6c9-cffe-3f71-aa40-eec3794b5795",
                                "text": "He had heard the stirring pibrochs speed the Gordons in their fights, / It had borne them through the fire zone as they swung up Dargai's heights […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d17d2e21-91aa-4b92-abea-bafee9dedb7f",
                                "sense_id": "758cb6c9-cffe-3f71-aa40-eec3794b5795",
                                "text": "Halfway through The Big Music, Kirsty Gunn notes that piobaireachd, a particular form of bagpipe composition, sounds ‘foreign and strange’ to those not raised on it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
